A||||9||fieroshop||Sunshade Covers and sunshades||||1||
Z||000000||fieroshop||05-17-2000||03:16 PM||||Well tomorrow I will find out the price of my new sunshades and sunshade covers. The sunshades will come in the stock six colors that the Fiero carried and the sunshades will be black with Fiero inscribtione on the bag. I will post pics. as soon as I have the covers here which will be hopefully tomorrow. If you are interested in one, e-mail me aff list.||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||05-17-2000||08:44 PM||||George,<P>Since the original sunshade bags tend to shrink, are you having the bag made slightly over the original size (say a 1/2" to 1") to compensate for the shrinkage? Also, are you making the sunshade out of the same fiberboard/cardboard material or are you planning to use a slightly thicker material that won't warp as easily? Also, any thought to making the sunshade board out of a waterproof material?<P>Also, when will they be ready to ship and how much are they?<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 05-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||05-17-2000||09:01 PM||||Tgowens, yes the bag will be a little larger all the way around and also it will be made out of a marine vinyl that will not shrink. I am also going to use a slightly heavier board so that the sunroof shade will not warp as the original. The bag will be identical to the oem bag. As far as the sunshade I still have to come up with either a plastic piece that goes around the sunroof handle or make it out of some other material.<BR>I went today to see how it was coming along and was told that they were waiting for the board to come in and they think it should be here sometime today or tomorrow. They are going to make the first bag and sunshade by tomorrow and I will know what kind of price we are looking at. Looks like I will be able to start shipping them sometime next week.||||reg||6
Z||000003||TOM||05-17-2000||10:10 PM||||I could mold the plastic piece from mine so you have some for the reproductions. but there is the small cost of materials. I was going to do some but no time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||05-17-2000||11:43 PM||||Are you going to offer a bracket for the cars that were pre sunshade. The sunroof handle is different and will need a bracket to hold the shade up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||05-18-2000||12:56 AM||||I have several sunshades that I can use and will use the plastic piece from one of them. As far as offering to the Fieros that did not come with them I was under the impression that all sunroofs were the same. Correct me if I am wrong but I did check the fit with some 84's and 85' as well as the later model years and they all seem to fit. But as usual I could be wrong and probably am. But what do I know.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 05-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||05-18-2000||02:32 PM||||Yes the panels are all the same but the latch is a little different. The shade cars has a small ledge on the front of the patch that the sunshade resta on. That is what the plastic thing is for ||||reg||1
Z||000007||AL||05-20-2000||01:21 PM||||what happened with the prices?||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroshop||05-22-2000||12:59 AM||||I went and saw what the shop did. They did not want to give me a price intil such time as they had done one and I come to find out that a. they do not want to do it and b. the price was so high tyhat nobody would buy them, and I would not want too sell them at such a high price. In order to come out ahead they would run in excess of $175.00. A little too steep for my pocket book and  most other people. I will keep looking for somebody to make them for me and will post my success or failure another time.||||reg||9
